      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5d100f3eb716313272a55e89|full_name}: They did have a standard height. Interacting with someone when you cant see their head or arm positions correctly makes things quite difficult. As I said before the world creator can enforce these restrictions or give the room master options to control how the game is played. Its not too difficult to detect height, it just depends on how they want to enforce it that could take a bit of time for some world creators. Beyond that I would venture to guess that the majority of players have wanted correct head and arm positions on blocked avatars for years.",
